      },
      "message": "fix(links): add the approach distance outside the stock for Inside and Outside passes\n\nAdd `approach_distance` (mm, default 2.0) to the operation's\n`links.approach`: how far outside the stock edge the entry of an Inside\nor Outside pass goes down, in air. A negative or non-finite value is\nrefused by name when the command is made. The project file writes the\nkey only when it is not the default (no version step; earlier files\nload the default), and the digest adds bytes only then. The Lead in /\nLead out page of 2D Offset, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive shows the\nApproach distance row when Pass starts at is Inside or Outside. MCP\nsets it through `links.approach.approach_distance`; the camcraft-mcp\nskill documents it. The entry that reads it is #3746.\n\nFixes #3745\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
